{
  "title": "Particle-in-cell / PIC",
  "html": "<h1>Particle-in-cell / PIC</h1><p>Plasma PIC represents a distribution by computational particles and self-consistent fields by a mesh. Its smoothing, collisionality and sampling error differ from direct all-pairs Coulomb dynamics.</p><h2 id=\"model\">Problem and representative equations</h2><p>Start with nonrelativistic electrostatic Vlasov–Poisson. Computational particle p has weight wₚ, charge qₚ and position xₚ. Dimensionless shape weights Sᵢ sum to one, and Vᵢ is cell volume. Deposit ρ, solve Poisson with the stated boundary conditions, and use E=−∇φ.</p><div class=\"math-block\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><munder><mo>∑</mo><mi>p</mi></munder><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">x</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"/><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∇</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"/><msub><mover accent=\"true\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">v</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">E</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">x</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho_i=\\frac1{V_i}\\sum_p w_pq_pS_i(\\mathbf x_p),\\qquad -\\nabla_h^2\\phi_i=\\rho_i/\\epsilon_0,\\qquad \\dot{\\mathbf v}_p=(q_p/m_p)\\mathbf E_h(\\mathbf x_p).</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">ρ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:2.7076em;vertical-align:-1.3861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.3214em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.314em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">V</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.2222em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.677em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.836em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mop op-limits\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.05em;\"><span style=\"top:-1.9em;margin-left:0em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.05em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.05em;\"></span><span><span class=\"mop op-symbol large-op\">∑</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.3861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0269em;\">w</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0269em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0576em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbf\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:2em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">∇</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8641em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.453em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">h</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.247em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">ϕ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0361em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">ρ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">ϵ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">0</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:2em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord katex-accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6813em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\" style=\"margin-right:0.016em;\">v</span></span><span style=\"top:-3.0134em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.1389em;\"><span class=\"mord\">˙</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.016em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0361em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbf\">E</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">h</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbf\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span></div><h2 id=\"algorithm\">Algorithm</h2><p>Repeat charge deposition, field solution, particle gathering and particle pushing; include background ions in ρ. Electromagnetic PIC additionally needs current deposition and Maxwell updates consistent with discrete continuity. Dawson’s sheet model is a historical particle-plasma example, not the definition of every PIC discretization.</p><h2 id=\"conditions\">Conditions and pitfalls</h2><p>Explicit electrostatic PIC must examine plasma-frequency time scales and Debye-length resolution. Exact restrictions depend on the particle pusher, shape and field solver. Separate sampling convergence in particle count from grid/time convergence, and check self-force and finite-grid heating.</p><p>The companion is one-dimensional periodic electrostatic cold-electron PIC with a fixed uniform ion background. It is a fixed CIC deposit/gather, Poisson-field and particle-push example; thermal Landau damping, electromagnetic PIC and moving ions are outside its scope.</p><h2 id=\"verification\">What to check</h2><p>Begin with single-particle self-force, a uniform neutral distribution, and small-amplitude plasma oscillations or Landau damping. Report charge, energy drift, particle-count dependence and independent random realizations. Compare damping rates only within the linear-amplitude regime used by the theory.</p><p>Use linear cold-plasma oscillation as a small-amplitude reference and vary mesh, time step and particle count separately. Report charge, field residual, self-force, particle momentum and particle-plus-field energy diagnostics separately. Small conservation diagnostics alone guarantee neither trajectory accuracy nor arbitrary long-time stability.</p><p>The companion also integrates the fixed CIC spatial system with DOP853 and tests tolerance/maximum-step sensitivity. This is an alternative time-integration algorithm, not an independent continuum Vlasov–Poisson solver. The random particle-count check concerns the initial power of one Fourier charge mode, compared with its analytic expectation including the finite-grid CIC response. It is distinct from particle-count convergence of arbitrary nonlinear trajectories.</p><h2 id=\"scoped-examples\">Check fixed inputs: separate scoped releases</h2><p>Check each example’s inputs, observables, diagnostic definitions and scope. What a passing check establishes depends on its acceptance criteria and differs from a general mathematical guarantee. Historical inputs, measurements and criteria are preserved.</p><article class=\"resource-summary\" id=\"supplement-pic\"><h3>Cold-plasma oscillation with electrostatic CIC PIC</h3><p>Computation for a fixed target</p><p>Couple electrons to a 1D periodic grid by CIC, solving Poisson and particle motion self-consistently.</p><p>Finite amplitude and finite particles leave an error floor. Nonlinear instabilities, Landau damping, collisions, electromagnetic/relativistic PIC and open particle boundaries are unvalidated.</p><p><a href=\"/numerical-methods-atlas/validation/pic/?lang=en\">Input, results and acceptance</a> · <a href=\"/numerical-methods-atlas/en/read/validation-particles/#pic\">Method, equations and sources</a> · <a href=\"https://hrkoyama.github.io/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particles/run.py\">Code: run.py</a> · <a href=\"https://hrkoyama.github.io/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particles/electrostatics.py\">Code: electrostatics.py</a> · <a href=\"https://hrkoyama.github.io/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particles/fmm.py\">Code: fmm.py</a> · <a href=\"https://hrkoyama.github.io/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particles/transport.py\">Code: transport.py</a> · <a href=\"https://hrkoyama.github.io/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particles/test_particles.py\">Tests: test_particles.py</a> · <a href=\"/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particles/atlas-particles-2026-11-22.zip\">Release ZIP</a> · <a href=\"/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particles/results/result.json\">Saved results</a> · <a href=\"/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particles/verification.json\">Independent-extraction rerun receipt</a></p></article><article class=\"resource-summary\" id=\"supplement-pic-conservation\"><h3>PIC: mesh/time convergence, invariants and particle noise</h3><p>Computation for a fixed target</p><p>Separate quiet-start refinement of a cold 1D periodic plasma from independent-seed initial particle noise; record charge, momentum, Gauss diagnostics and energy error.</p><p>DOP853 is not an independent PIC spatial implementation. Distinguish charge/momentum preservation from approximate energy conservation. Initial-noise N scaling does not validate evolved warm plasmas. Landau damping, electromagnetic/relativistic PIC and collisions remain unvalidated.</p><p><a href=\"/numerical-methods-atlas/validation/pic-conservation/?lang=en\">Input, results and acceptance</a> · <a href=\"/numerical-methods-atlas/en/read/validation-particle-transport/#pic-conservation\">Method, equations and sources</a> · <a href=\"https://hrkoyama.github.io/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particle-transport/run.py\">Code: run.py</a> · <a href=\"https://hrkoyama.github.io/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particle-transport/kinetic_experiments.py\">Code: kinetic_experiments.py</a> · <a href=\"https://hrkoyama.github.io/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particle-transport/kinetics.py\">Code: kinetics.py</a> · <a href=\"https://hrkoyama.github.io/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particle-transport/longrange_experiments.py\">Code: longrange_experiments.py</a> · <a href=\"https://hrkoyama.github.io/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particle-transport/electrostatics.py\">Code: electrostatics.py</a> · <a href=\"https://hrkoyama.github.io/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particle-transport/fmm.py\">Code: fmm.py</a> · <a href=\"https://hrkoyama.github.io/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particle-transport/test_kinetics.py\">Tests: test_kinetics.py</a> · <a href=\"https://hrkoyama.github.io/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particle-transport/test_longrange.py\">Tests: test_longrange.py</a> · <a href=\"https://hrkoyama.github.io/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particle-transport/test_runner.py\">Tests: test_runner.py</a> · <a href=\"/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particle-transport/atlas-particle-transport-2026-11-22.zip\">Release ZIP</a> · <a href=\"/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particle-transport/results/result.json\">Saved results</a> · <a href=\"/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particle-transport/verification.json\">Independent-extraction rerun receipt</a></p></article><h2 id=\"publication-scope\">Publication scope and related entries</h2><p>The historical reading, equations, sources and release are preserved; a separate companion release supplies bounded checks for fixed conditions. This does not mean every general verification suggestion above has been executed. Consult each release’s dedicated page and saved record for inputs, references, checks and limits.</p><ul><li><a href=\"/numerical-methods-atlas/methods/pic/?lang=en\">Particle-in-cell / PIC</a></li></ul><h2 id=\"sources\">Primary publications, supporting sources and review scope</h2><p>Distinguish original research, later variants, author monographs, pedagogical articles and official references. Bibliographic verification differs from consulting selected passages; neither implies a full-paper audit or numerical reproduction. Access-depth notes accompany each source.</p><ol class=\"reading-sources\"><li id=\"source-dawson1962\"><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1706638\">John Dawson (1962). One-Dimensional Plasma Model</a>. The Physics of Fluids<p>Research publication: proposal or related formulation · Bibliography checked · <a href=\"https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1063%2F1.1706638\">Consulted record</a></p><p>Bibliographic identity checked against the DOI registration on 2026-11-22. Relevant abstracts or selected passages are separately identified in the detailed-reading source notes; this is not a claim of a full-paper audit or numerical reproduction.</p></li><li id=\"source-hockney1981book\"><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1201/9780367806934\">Hockney, R. W. and Eastwood, J. W. (1981). Computer Simulation Using Particles</a>. McGraw-Hill<p>Author monograph / supporting reference · Bibliography checked · <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1201/9780367806934\">Consulted record</a></p><p>Original book date is 1981, as cited by Barnes and Hut (1986); DOI identifies a later Taylor &amp; Francis reissue. Reference for particle-mesh methods and isolated doubled-domain convolution; the self-cell kernel convention is stated separately in our code.</p></li></ol>",
